
Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount != Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);
</code>

This output is correct as the PUT_RemoveContract method removes an element from an ArrayList and the Count property of the ArrayList should decrease by 1 every time an element is removed. If the count stays the same as the last index of x in the new ArrayList, it means that the element never existed in the ArrayList.
